.TH as "" "Command"
.SH NAME
as \- assembler for host computer
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBas [\-glx] [\-o \fIdest\fB] \fIfile ...\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
as -- assembler for host computer
Usage:	as [ options ] file ...
Options:
	-g	Make all undefined symbols global
	-l	Output listing to standard output
	-o dest	Rename output file 'dest' (default: 'l.out')
	-x	Strip local symbols from symbol table
.HE
.B as
is the COHERENT assembler for the host machine (the Zilog Z8001).
It assembles one or more
.I file
arguments into a single relocatable object module, suitable for
linking by
.BR ld ,
by default named
.BR l.out .
Options and file names may be given in any order.
.PP
.B as
recognizes the following options:
.IP \fB\-g\fR
Make every symbol that is referenced but never defined in this
assembly global, so the linker will look for its definition in
another module.
.IP \fB\-l\fR
Write an assembly listing to the standard output.
.IP \fB\-o\ \fIdest\fR
Write the assembled object module into
.I dest
instead of
.BR l.out .
.IP \fB\-x\fR
Strip local (non-global) symbols from the symbol table written into
the output object module.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.B cc ,
.B ld
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B as
prints a message on the standard error for each erroneous line and,
if any errors are found, exits with a nonzero status without
producing a usable object module.
